5e3213-66d9-5042-96df-93870211d6aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-83746" :question/problem "Which of the following are discrete random variables?\n\n- The number of hearts in a standard deck of cards\n- The number of diamonds obtained when $7$ cards are randomly selected from a standard deck of cards\n- The number of times a card is selected from a standard deck of cards until a King appears" :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\nA *discrete* random variable is a random variable\n\n- that has finitely many possible values, or\n\n- whose possible values can be listed in a sequence: ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},…$\n\nRemember that a real interval (e.g. $(a,b)$ or $[a,b]$) cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a discrete random variable. The number of hearts in a particular complete deck of cards is not the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\n- Statement II describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values can be listed in a sequence: $0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7.$\n\n- Statement III describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and we can count its possible values in a sequence: $1,2,3,…$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83746/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f7256c7-afea-5c33-a859-623b0531e88c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83746"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83761/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "eff4a979-10a7-5ebe-bd4d-70dc5129cf5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83761/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "6017175a-b713-5849-9fb4-6e903d4a6a93" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83761/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "b73762ed-d70e-505e-83c9-a45a7bb49679" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83761/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "e4c0cc6f-bd17-5d4d-9a59-e2f52551ace2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83761/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "70acd9eb-db10-59f5-9f24-6577e58acdf5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83761/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15bd96ad-d876-5a6d-b5da-db132950ed3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83761/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-83761/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-83761/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-83761/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-83761/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-83761/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83761" :question/id #uuid "f10ce05b-98d5-5803-ada2-520a875a4943" :question/math-academy-id "q-83761" :question/problem "Which of the following are discrete random variables?\n\n- The weight of a randomly selected student\n- The amount of water in a randomly selected student's water bottle\n- The number of books borrowed by a randomly selected library user in a particular month" :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\nA *discrete* random variable is a random variable\n\n- that has finitely many possible values, or\n\n- whose possible values can be listed in a sequence: ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},…$\n\nRemember that a real interval (e.g. $(a,b)$ or $[a,b]$) cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a discrete random variable. Although its value is determined by the result of an experiment, the possible values are real numbers that cannot be listed in a sequence.\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a discrete random variable. Although its value is determined by the result of an experiment, we cannot list the possible real-numbered values in a sequence.\n\n- Statement III describes a discrete random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and it has finitely many possible values: $0,1,2,3,…$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83761/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f7256c7-afea-5c33-a859-623b0531e88c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83761"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125075/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "d073bbc1-76bd-5baf-9bad-ad3e51fa4c64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125075/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "161d95cf-2985-5e9f-9993-fbe1089d2210" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125075/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348